FILE     ../../fanuc_macros/programs/p045_O1001.nc (from line 36)
DIALECT  series 0 (given)
NOTE     drilling cycles are written out as moves; cycle values in D20 D22 D23 D24 D25
NOTE     G43/G49 left out: the DX32 applies the tool length of the tool in the spindle from its table (TENTATIVE)
NOTE     T without M6 left out: the DX32 takes T in the M6 block
NOTE     -ftool 1: T1 must be in the spindle when the program starts
NOTE     G84 without P (or P below 50): the DX32 G84 dwells at least .05 s at the bottom and at R, where FANUC does not dwell
NOTE     G84 written as the DX32 G84, plug reverse tapping: the tap needs a floating holder, and the spindle speed and feed must suit it (DX32 manual fig. 5-3) (-tap float)
NOTE     G28 X/Y go to the intermediate point only (-g28xy stay): the DX32 has no X/Y reference return; check the program is safe there
NOTE     G28 Z written as M25, the DX32 quill home (TENTATIVE: check that it goes where FANUC's reference point is) (-g28)
NOTE     1 called program(s) written as DX32 macros #1-#1, nested 1 deep
NOTE     the output needs BOSS 4-7 compatibility mode off
WROTE    dxtk.txt
CHECK    dxsim reads dxtk.txt cleanly and reaches all 52 FANUC end points in order
RESULT   ok
